@@ -0,0 +1,28 @@
+# Private J714s normal-boot candidate
+
+This prepares the existing Omarchy m1n1 and U-Boot package recipes with the public sources that boot Edimoldovan's J714c through stage 1 → ESP stage 2 → U-Boot → Limine → EFI Linux. It is a developer candidate for adapting that chain to J714s, not a supported installer, a complete image or hardware qualification. It is deliberately outside `pkgbuilds/`, so normal package discovery, build matrices and publication do not select it. The prepared copies have their publication/watch metadata removed.
+
+```bash
+candidates/j714s-normal-boot/prepare /absolute/new/build-directory
+```
+
+The command copies the recipes from immutable omacom/omarchy-pkgs commit `30a33ee435db8f4a158ca41f82e91cc34bcd2e3b`, verifies and applies `recipes.patch`, then checks the recipe syntax and existing build-only qualification validator. It does not fetch source, build packages, touch a Mac, register a helper, enroll stage 1 or publish anything. Existing output directories are refused. Build the generated recipes with the ordinary Arch `makepkg` tooling in an appropriate aarch64 build environment; both retain their established package names and conflict/provider relationships, so do not install them on an ordinary supported Mac.
+
+## Source and packaging
+
+| Component | Exact public source | What is retained |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| m1n1 | [edimoldovan/m1n1 `bafef4b456a98c0a8966b4d9502d55694d2e4c9b`](https://github.com/edimoldovan/m1n1/commit/bafef4b456a98c0a8966b4d9502d55694d2e4c9b) | Original recipe's artwork, Clang/lld and Rust 1.89.0 build, separate stage 1 and `ESP_STAGE2=1` builds, installer compatibility files, licenses and ordinary asahi-scripts hook dependency. Stage 1 is never enrolled by this recipe. |
+| U-Boot | [edimoldovan/u-boot `70e990818a895454780797beedc6a7bdac9e2fd6`](https://github.com/edimoldovan/u-boot/commit/70e990818a895454780797beedc6a7bdac9e2fd6) | Original recipe's silent-console patch, `EFI_RT_VOLATILE_STORE`, asahi-boot payload path, conflicts/providers and GPL license installation. The source adopts a live ANS session only when m1n1 supplies `asahi,nvme-adopt`. |
+
+The local version suffix `.j714s1` distinguishes these artifacts from the official package versions. The m1n1 qualification record remains `hardware_tested=false`. These pins are candidates derived from a J714c report; neither the exact combined pair nor this packaging is claimed to have booted J714s. The report is [omacom/linux-aurora#293, Nov 7](https://github.com/omacom/linux-aurora/issues/293#issuecomment-6712674405); the upstream loader submission is [omacom/m1n1#30](https://github.com/omacom/m1n1/pull/30). Authors and source licenses remain those of the pinned projects; no source patch is rewritten or relabeled as our hardware discovery.
+
+## Before this can become an installer profile
+
+- Qualify the exact loader pair with a matching J714s EFI-capable kernel, device tree, modules and GPU userspace. This candidate deliberately changes no kernel recipe or public model catalog.
+- Match the selected stub restore OS to macOS 27.3 beta 1 / build `26C5035r`, and verify the actual system/stub boot-firmware identity `mBoot-20457.60.65.0.1` separately. Updating the main macOS alone does not establish the stub's firmware identity. The installer worker's proposed `qualified_system_firmware` check is not yet emitted by the production image builder.
+- Qualify cold boot, warm restart, complete poweroff, first login, ordinary kernel/DTB/U-Boot update recomposition and recovery. Preserve existing-model qualification before any shared recipe is changed.
+- Adopt the ordinary SMC poweroff driver only after J714s DT/nvmem review. [Edimoldovan's `38e75c9f1c07`](https://github.com/edimoldovan/linux-aurora/commit/38e75c9f1c07) enables the existing SMC reboot node and `CONFIG_POWER_RESET_MACSMC`; it is not a new driver and is not included here. Its J714c PMIC scratchpad claims do not qualify another board.
+- Provision required Apple firmware privately through the installer's authenticated preparation path. No firmware, tickets, per-unit ADT, passwords or signed release credentials are supplied here.
+
+Do not promote these recipes or add J714s to a signed release catalog on the strength of a package build. A build and the J714c author's hardware result are separate evidence from a complete fresh install on J714s.
