+# Native ARM64 Mesa build, without touching the Mac
+
+The established package workflow already has the required route: `.github/workflows/build-pr.yml` accepts a manual `workflow_dispatch` with `packages=mesa-aurora`, uses `ubuntu-24.04-arm` for aarch64 userspace and runs the ordinary Arch Linux ARM container builder. Its result is an unsigned, tree-hash-labelled `packages.tar` Actions artifact. It does not sign, release, promote, update a channel or admit a model. The publishing workflow is separate and must remain disabled on the source-only fork.
+
+Use two branches in the owner's fork:
+
+1. The integration branch keeps standard `pkgbuilds/` untouched and contains this private preparer/snapshot.
+2. A build-only `codex/j714s-mesa-native-build` branch starts from that exact reviewed integration commit and copies only the generated `mesa-aurora/PKGBUILD` and `j714s-gpu.env` into `pkgbuilds/mesa-aurora/`. Preserve that directory's existing metadata so the normal build resolver can select it. This branch is an explicit build input, never a promotion request or a change to the fork's default branch.
+
+Review the two-file overlay, record its source commit and `git rev-parse HEAD:pkgbuilds/mesa-aurora`, enable only `build-pr.yml`, then dispatch:
+
+```bash
+gh workflow run build-pr.yml --repo TripleU613/omarchy-pkgs --ref codex/j714s-mesa-native-build -f packages=mesa-aurora
+```
+
+Do not enable or dispatch `publish.yml`, push these recipes to `master`, or use an artifact's existence as GPU qualification. The existing workflow retains seven-day build artifacts and meson failure logs; download them promptly, verify the selected source/tree identity, package architecture, dependencies and ELF targets, then pass actual package hashes through the normal authenticated candidate/image producer. `.BUILDINFO`, `.PKGINFO` and the CI job logs identify the real tools/dependencies. Check the completed jobs; a queued run or an uploaded failure log is not a successful build.
+
+This host currently cannot use the existing local container path: its Docker socket is unavailable to the current user; Podman is not installed; QEMU registration has `PF` rather than the `F`+`C` flags the repository requires for rootless container sudo. No permission or binfmt bypass is part of this candidate.
+
+GitHub's [standard runner documentation](https://docs.github.com/en/actions/how-tos/write-workflows/choose-where-workflows-run/choose-the-runner-for-a-job) currently lists the public ARM64 runner as 4 CPU/16 GB and standard public-repository compute as free. Private repositories use their account's included/billed minutes. The existing workflow caps a job at 180 minutes; this candidate's actual native Mesa duration has not been measured.
